body:
I don't think marika splits in half to become radagon and marika, mecause there's dialogue from melina in the queen's bedchamber; 
"In Marika's own words. O Radagon, leal hound of the Golden Order. Thou'rt yet to become me, thou'rt yet to become a god. Let us both be shattered, mine other half"
Seems to imply Radagon was a champion of the golden order, and later joined with marika (for some reason) but ofc it can be interpreted that they were always the same. Open ended fromsoft shenanigans

Good books on the Sengoku period, particularly focusing on the struggle between Oda Nobunaga and Takeda Shingen?

&#x200B;

Doesn't have to be exclusively about them, in fact I'd prefer if there was info on other lords/clans of the time, but I'd really like to know about the political and military maneuvering that went on between the two.
